Student: Chaplin Marchais
Date   : 11/14/26
Project: SMSH Project 5

Summary:
    smsh is a small command shell that runs interactively, reads a script, or
    executes a command supplied with -c. Build it with make. Run ./smsh for the
    interactive prompt, ./smsh scriptfile to read commands from a file, or
    ./smsh -c command ... to execute the joined command arguments.

    External commands run in child processes. The shell also provides these
    built-ins:
         NAME=value  store a shell variable
         set         list stored variables (exported variables are marked)
         export NAME include a variable in child-process environments
         cd [PATH]   change the current directory (HOME when PATH is omitted)
         read NAME  read a line from standard input into a variable
         exit [N]   exit with status N, or with the last command result

    Variable substitutions include $NAME, $$ (the shell process ID), and $?
    (the last command result). The shell also supports inline command
    substitution with $(command), comments beginning with an unescaped #,
    backslash escaping, and basic if/then/else/fi conditional blocks. Script
    arguments after the filename are stored in positional variables named
    1, 2, and so on.

    Command lines are split on spaces and tabs. Quoting, pipelines, and
    input/output redirection are not implemented. Inline command output is
    captured and inserted into the command line, with newlines converted to
    spaces.

Files:
    smsh.c        -- initialization, input-mode selection, and main loop
    process.c     -- command dispatch, child-process execution, and output capture
    process.h     -- command-processing function declarations
    builtin.c     -- built-ins, assignments, comments, and substitutions
    builtin.h     -- built-in and substitution function declarations
    controlflow.c -- if/then/else/fi state and conditional execution
    controlflow.h -- control-flow function declarations
    varlib.c      -- shell variable storage and child environment management
    varlib.h      -- variable-library function declarations
    splitline2.c  -- command-line reading, tokenization, and argument cleanup
    splitline2.h  -- command-reading and parsing function declarations
    flexstr2.c    -- dynamically growing string and string-list helpers
    flexstr2.h    -- flexible string/list structures and declarations
    smsh.h        -- shared shell declarations
    Makefile      -- builds smsh; make clean removes object files and executable
    Plan          -- design document for the project
